TEXT -472 -416 Left 2 ;Use the internal measurement of the synchronousgenerator instead
TEXT -560 -152 Left 2 ;See also the influence of damper winding\nDisable damping by setting RDx and RDy to 1e6\n(now the damper currents goes to zero)\nYou see that the speed of gen. has now fluctuations\nTo enable damping again delete RDx RDy parameters in the \nparameter line of the synchronous machine
TEXT -800 -80 Left 2 ;You can see that the current shortly after t=10s is very high\nThis is due to the decrease of Xd from Xd to Xd'' at the begin of the fault\nThe terminal voltage goes to zero\nThe load angle to 90 degrees and the speed of the generator decrease\nThe speed decrease because the generator has no speed controller\nTherefore the energy needed by the generator is fed by the inertia of the generator
TEXT -656 -272 Left 2 ;RE = UE0/IE0 is rather high (default)\nTo set RE lower change UE0 from 600 to 100\nAlso verr voltage source should now be set to about 100V instead 600V\nRE influence the time constant of the magn. field circuit\nYou can see it by plotting the magn.field current \n(By clicking the current at F1 input of the machine)
